{#- /robots.txt — a template rather than a file in public/, because the Sitemap line
   must carry an absolute URL and the origin differs between production and the
   GitHub Pages staging build (SITE_ORIGIN in eleventy.config.ts).

   Until this existed, /robots.txt was the single most-requested URL the site did not
   serve: 6,222 direct 404s in a 30-day window, plus 5,174 more arriving at the legacy
   WWU hostname and being swept into the redirect handler, where they crowded the real
   legacy URLs out of the #181 mapping queue.

   Nothing is disallowed, deliberately. /analytics/ and /curation/ are unlinked
   internal pages kept out of search by `robots: noindex` in their front matter, and a
   crawler can only obey a meta tag on a page it is allowed to fetch — disallowing
   them here would leave them indexable by any crawler that found them some other way.
-#}
